From: JamesDSP root fork - 0008
Subject: [PATCH 0008] engine: mix fidelity self check (catch a replace style write
 over the shared mix without the vendor PCM dump)

Patch 0005 fixed a real, user visible bug: with EFFECT_BUFFER_ACCESS_ACCUMULATE
the effect's out buffer is the output thread's *shared mix*, so the contract is
"add your rendered output to it".  The engine used to store over it, which
deleted every other session's contribution (one session playing made the next
one silent).  That bug was only visible in a thread level capture - the vendor
AF40_ThreadWrite dump, see docs/TAP-AUDIO-LOSS-VERIFICATION.md - because each
per-instance lane still looks healthy while another chain's audio disappears.

This patch turns the contract into a counter that runs inside the engine, so
any ROM can assert it without any vendor dump:

    out_after == out_before + rendered        (saturating for int16/int32)

The process path snapshots the shared mix right before the accumulate, compares
it afterwards and counts the buffers that do not match.  The counters are
process wide (every instance in audioserver adds to them) and are exposed
through the diagnostic parameter channel:

  30023 GET  broken buffers (overwrote somebody else's mix)   <- must stay 0
  30024 GET  checked buffers                                  <- must grow
  30025 SET  arm (1) / disarm (0)
  30026 SET  reset the counters
  30027 GET  armed flag
  30028 GET  mismatching samples in the last broken buffer

Default state is OFF and the unarmed path is one relaxed atomic load plus a
predictable branch: no allocation, no memcpy, no log, no counter update.  The
snapshot buffer is allocated lazily the first time the check is armed, per
engine instance, and freed with the instance.  The diagnostic ids are handled
before the write-lock gate and before the parameter classifier, so they need no
engine key, are never queued, never persisted and never reach the DSP.

Modes covered: float32, int32 and int16.  Packed 24 bit and int8_24 keep the
historical replace behaviour (patch 0005) and are deliberately not checked -
the check never claims fidelity it did not verify.

Host tests: native/test/test_mixcheck.c (the two real bug shapes - replace over
a non-zero mix and a silent holder wiping the thread - plus saturation and the
arm/reset accounting).

Overhead measured on this device: see docs/ENGINE-TAP-AND-MIX-CHECK.md.
---
